@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Projection WL — deterministic labels to structural clone candidates

rectangle "GraphProjection\nsorted NodeId universe\nforward + reverse CSR" as INPUT #F1F3F5
rectangle "Validate complete projection\nnode order · CSR shape · bounds\nweights aligned · reverse agreement" as VALIDATE #FFE8CC
rectangle "Directed-degree seed\n<latex>\ell_0(v)=mix(mix(A,d^-(v)),d^+(v))</latex>" as SEED #DBE4FF
rectangle "Clamp refinement rounds\n<latex>k=min(requested,16)</latex>" as CAP #FFF3BF
rectangle "Collect incident labels\nincoming + outgoing multiset" as COLLECT #D3F9D8
rectangle "Sort multiset and fold\nfixed wrapping SplitMix combiner" as MIX #C3FAE8
rectangle "Canonicalize whole round\nsorted distinct raw hash rank" as CANON #E5DBFF
rectangle "Final Vec<u64>\naligned with projection nodes" as LABELS #C3FAE8
rectangle "Group equal labels\nretain size >= max(min_class,2)" as GROUP #FCC2D7
rectangle "Ordered Vec<Vec<NodeId>>\nmembers ascending\nsize descending · smallest id" as CLONES #FCC2D7
rectangle "Empty result\nmalformed projection" as EMPTY #FFE3E3

INPUT --> VALIDATE
VALIDATE --> EMPTY : invalid
VALIDATE --> SEED : valid
SEED --> CAP
CAP --> LABELS : k = 0
CAP --> COLLECT : next round
COLLECT --> MIX
MIX --> CANON
CANON --> COLLECT : another round
CANON --> LABELS : k rounds complete
LABELS --> GROUP
GROUP --> CLONES

note right of CANON
  Sorting raw values before assigning ranks
  preserves numeric labels under an
  isomorphic stable-identifier relabeling.
end note

note bottom of CLONES
  Equal WL labels are candidate evidence.
  They do not prove exact isomorphism
  or behavioral equivalence.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#F1F3F5>| payload-free graph input |
  |<#FFE8CC>| structural validation |
  |<#DBE4FF>| directed seed |
  |<#FFF3BF>| resource bound |
  |<#D3F9D8>| neighborhood collection |
  |<#C3FAE8>| deterministic hashing or labels |
  |<#E5DBFF>| graph-wide canonicalization |
  |<#FCC2D7>| clone grouping and result |
  |<#FFE3E3>| explicit invalid outcome |
endlegend
@enduml
